 ## Permissions
 
-Admin settings require `manage_options`. The public Create button appears only when the logged-in user has `edit_posts` and belongs to a configured allowed role. Default allowed roles are `administrator` and `editor`. The shell never grants publishing capabilities.
+Admin settings require `manage_options`. File 20 never grants publishing capabilities.
+
+The version 1.0.1 Create producer contract keeps login, Safe Mode, and Emergency Disable non-overridable. Its legacy fallback requires `edit_posts` plus a configured allowed role. File 22 may replace only that legacy presentation result through `sabri_shell_can_show_create` after its Membership Core, capability, adapter, and current-availability checks.
+
+Desktop and mobile Create surfaces use the same final authorization decision. An explicit mobile `create` setting cannot bypass it.
+
+Read-only producer functions:
+
+```php
+sabri_shell_create_contract_available();
+sabri_shell_create_visible_for_current_user();
+```
+
+File 21 must preserve its native fallback unless both functions confirm the complete current-user gateway.
